From a98c4be1752e35d6b791a1f11be2a2aa425c7be7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ewan McIntyre <ewan3568@me.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:56:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Trip builder backend: free to send, pay after approval

Sending a trip for checking no longer takes a $50 per person deposit (Ewan, 23 Oct 2026). The guest pays only after
the crew has checked the trip and set the price.

- trip-builder-request: saves the trip as "submitted" and emails the crew and the guest at once. No Stripe, no payment
  link. The bed hold starts now. The old deposit is a switch: the secret TRIP_BUILDER_DEPOSIT_PER_PERSON (unset, 0 or
  anything that isn't 1-1000 means free; a number brings the deposit back). Trips that already paid one are untouched.
- Paying: with no deposit there is no card on file, so one is saved as part of choosing. Instalments: the first
  payment's Checkout also saves the card. "A week before I leave": a Checkout page in setup mode saves a card (nothing
  charged), and stripe-webhook (new kind trip_builder_card) books them when it is saved, only if the trip is still
  'ready' at the price they were shown; otherwise the card is kept, nothing is booked and Ewan is told.
- The crew can act on a free trip (no deposit to wait for), the review page suggests the whole trip cost as the price,
  and every email reads correctly when nothing was paid up front. New guest email: "Your trip is with the crew".
- Open to anyone now, so: the first email prints only a plain first name and a route that reads as a route, the log-in
  email too, and a guest changing a trip nobody on the crew has picked up gets no confirmation email.
- Log in finds free trips; the status answer gains canPay; the admin screen and the test send show free trips.
- public/trip-builder/config.js: DEPOSIT_PER_PERSON 50 -> 0.

No migration (deposit_amount is 0 on a free trip). Tests: 58 Deno (10 new), end-to-end 114 -> 157 checks (the deposit flow
still passes with the switch on; the free flow, the card page, a price that changes meanwhile, no card from Stripe, the
junk-text cases). See docs/trip-builder-free-send.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
